Q: Update dataGridView when cell value changed A: <p>Try to add following action to CellValueChanged event on your DataGridView.</p>

<pre><code>private void dataGridView1_CellValueChanged(object sender, DataGridViewCellEventArgs e)
{
        var grid = (sender as DataGridView);
        if (e.RowIndex != -1 &amp;&amp; (e.ColumnIndex == 0 || e.ColumnIndex == 1))
            (grid.Rows[e.RowIndex]).Cells[2].Value = (int)(grid.Rows[e.RowIndex]).Cells[0].Value + (int)(grid.Rows[e.RowIndex]).Cells[1].Value;
}
</code></pre>

<p>It checks if first or second column was changed and if this change is for any possible row.
It should update 3rd column based on values in 1st and 2nd column for that one row where you changed these column values.
Right now it only works for integer values.</p>
